Description:
**Job Title:** Security Lead Supervisor  
**Reports To:** Account Manager  
**Location:** Scarborough

**Schedule**

* Monday to Thursday 11am to 7pm
* Sunday 1pm to 9pm
* Friday/Saturday OFF

**Primary Focus:**

* The Security Lead Supervisor working with the Manager’s Security Manager and Assistant Manager at the Property shall be expected to lead the Property in reaching the goals and objectives that have been iterated throughout this Agreement. This position is one of leadership, customer service, extensive emergency management experience, and outstanding diplomacy skills.

* The Security Lead Supervisor is responsible for day-to-day supervision of the security and life safety program at the Property, and the provision of the Security and Life Safety Services at the Property. Working with the Manager’s Security Manager and Assistant Manager, this supervisory position is tasked with managing all of the Contractor’s responsibilities under this Agreement. The Security Lead Supervisor shall focus attention on maintaining company standards and industry best practice in the areas of Emergency Management, Operational Management, Personnel & Staffing, Budget & Administration, Health & Safety and other relevant Security & Life Safety Department functions. A critical component of this position is quality assurance to ensure overall compliance with required standards.

* The Security Lead Supervisor shall establish and maintain key contacts with internal, tenant, public authority, supplier, and security industry stakeholders. The position shall also help to set goals for the Contractor’s Personnel at the Property and ensure they are achieved, and shall focus on performance management and individual development in support of continued high standards and effective succession planning. The Security Lead Supervisor shall liaise regularly with the Manager’s Security Manager and Assistant Security Manager at the Property and provide input to future planning and major security-related projects at the Property. A significant responsibility of this role is participation in the preparation, upkeep and testing of emergency response plans to ensure the Property is adequately prepared to deal with a wide range of potentially adverse incidents.

**Essential Duties and Responsibilities:**

* Emergency Management
* Operational Management
* Personnel and Staffing
* Budget and Administration
* Fire, Health and Safety

**Key Contacts:**

**Internal:** The Manager’s Security Manager and Assistant Security Manager at the Property, Contractor’s Personnel, the general manager(s) at the Property and the Manager’s operations, marketing and guest services personnel

**External:** Key tenant stakeholders, police and emergency services contacts, transit authority contacts, municipal and provincial authorities, industry association members, professional security industry contacts, suppliers and contractors.

**Supervisory Responsibilities:**

The Security Lead Supervisor shall direct the day-to-day activities of all the Contractor’s Personnel at the Property. The Security Lead Supervisor shall help to establish and maintain an effective and professional workforce by focusing on:

* (1) hiring candidates with knowledge, skills and abilities to perform specified duties and responsibilities;
* (2) training to a high standard;
* (3) mentoring and motivating;
* (4) equal and ethical treatment;
* (5) recognition and reward;
* (6) leading by example.

**Education and/or Experience:**

* In addition to completion of the grade 12 certificate, a community college diploma (or equivalent business management qualification) in a security/life safety, risk management or criminology-related discipline is preferred or equivalent level of mature security experience;
* Completion of a supervisory management program upon assignment to the account;
* Three (3) years working in a commercial real estate security environment, in positions of increasing responsibility – or equivalent work experience; and
* One (1) year of security supervisory experience, ideally at one of the Manager’s Properties or a property of comparably complex scope (i.e. large, mixed-use facility) – or equivalent work experience.

**Supervisory Management Program: (Sample topics to be covered).**

* Fire detection, suppression and life safety / Occupational Health & Safety
* Hazard Identification and Risk Assessment (HIRA)
* Accident prevention, investigation, and ergonomics / Traffic control
* Emergency response
* Human, public and media relations / Private security and police relations
* Arrest, Use-of-Force, Confinement and Restraints
* Effective assertion and de-escalation / Customer Service
* Protection of crime scenes & preserving evidence
* Interview techniques / Search & Seizure / Information privacy
* Report Writing / Legal authority of a security guard / Courtroom testimony
* Telephone procedures and etiquette / Radio procedures and etiquette
* Controlled substances / abnormal behavior
* Protective alarm systems / Access Control / Patrol vehicle driver safety
* Active Shooters / Violence in the workplace / Bomb threats / Terrorism

**Technical Skills:**

* Knowledge of the duties and responsibilities of all direct and indirect reports;
* Understands property management and property security and life safety needs;
* Good working knowledge of Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Google products;
* Knowledge of security and life safety technology (i.e. CCTV, access control, fire alarm, intrusion) and other security-related systems;
* Knowledge and understanding of applicable federal, provincial and municipal legislation and regulations in the area of security and life safety management;
* Sound knowledge of industry techniques and emergent trends in security and life safety

**Interpersonal Skills:**

* Excellent written and verbal communication skills;
* Ability to motivate, coach and mentor;
* Strong analytical, problem solving and decision-making skills;
* Strong organizational, prioritization and time management skills;
* Tact and diplomacy in dealings at all levels of the organization;
* Ability to work in a challenging, fast-paced, multi-tasked environment;
* Flexible and adaptable in dealing with diverse situations and people;
* Good public speaking and presentation skills in group settings;
* Ability to delegate and empower effectively; and
* Team player.

**Functional Responsibilities:**

**Emergency Management:**

* Contribute to and maintain the Manager’s emergency management plans including the Fire Safety Plan, Emergency Response Plan (including Evacuation Plan) and Business Continuity Plan;
* Ensure emergency contact lists (i.e. staff, tenants, suppliers, authorities) are maintained and up-to-date;
* Liaise regularly with the Manager’s tenants in relation to emergency preparedness and response;
* Ensure the Contractor’s Personnel are trained in and aware of relevant emergency-related protocols at the Property;
* Function as the “Incident Commander” in the event of an emergency, reporting to property management.

**Operational Management:**

* Direct responsibility for supervising the Contractor’s Personnel at the Property.
* Ongoing coordination to ensure all aspects of the security and life safety program at the Property are assessed and updated regularly to remain current with the Manager’s Standard Operating Procedures and industry best practice, and to continually achieve operational and fiscal efficiency;
* Develop and maintain operational procedures, processes and standards to facilitate ongoing and effective security and life safety management practices and ensure these procedures are updated as required;
* Provide ongoing support and counsel to the Manager’s tenants at the Property on security-related issues;
* Establish, maintain and leverage key, property-level and strategic contacts (internal and external) and through regular interaction, provide and maintain timely accurate support as required to ensure open communication and the provision of the Security and Life Safety Services of a high level at the Property;
* Implementation and management of security and life safety related work projects, with an emphasis on continuous improvement and maximization of value;
* Contribute to, guide and maintain an all-inclusive five year security and life safety management plan;
* Maintain positive and constructive relationships with internal contacts (i.e. the general manager(s) at the Property, team department heads etc.) by providing timely and accurate support as required to ensure open communication is fostered between all levels of management;
* Create and deliver presentations from time to time to tenants, internal and other stakeholder groups;
* Review security incident reports and identify adverse incident trends. Take follow up actions as necessary;
* Respond to calls for service and security-related incidents as required, and conduct other operational duties as assigned by the Manager’s Security Manager and Assistant Security Manager at the Property; and
* Work closely and in conjunction with the Manager’s Security Manager and Assistant Security Manager at the Property and the Contractor’s Personnel to design, implement and evaluate security and safety measures at the Property, as well as to assist the Manager in developing control procedures and practices to enhance and improve those that are set out in the Service Specifications and the Individual Property Specifications.

**Personnel and Staffing:**

* Set individual and team objectives within the Contractor’s Personnel as reviewed by the Manager’s Security Manager and Assistant Security Manager at the Property, and personally ensure these are achieved to a high and consistent standard;
* Provide mentoring and support to the Contractor’s Personnel at the Property with a view to maintaining high standards of security and life safety management practice and overall succession planning;
* Planning of all of the Contractor’s Personnel training and education as required under this Agreement and otherwise consistent with industry standards.

**Budget and Administration:**

* Work to optimize revenues and expenditures to leverage maximum value for the Manager at the Property;
* Prepare, review, distribute and file daily memoranda, staff records, correspondence and other pertinent communications;
* Review invoices as requested, and submit requests for payment for Security and Life Safety Services rendered;
* Prepare, recommend and implement and monitor new revenue-generating or cost-cutting ideas for the provision of security and life safety at the Property.

**Health and Safety:**

* Be a member of the Manager’s Joint Health & Safety Committee (JH&SC) and support the JH&SC program to ensure occupational safety is prioritized and effectively practiced throughout all areas of operations at the Property;
* Ensure the Contractor’s Personnel are properly qualified, experienced and trained to be classified as "competent workers" as defined by provincial legislation;
* Assist the Manager’s Joint Health and Safety Committee (where required by Manager) in conducting accident investigations and organizing necessary training courses for employees;
* Level 1 & 2 Health & Safety Certification; and
* Maintain a program of regular inspections and risk assessments in common areas and tenant leased premises at the Property for the purposes of identifying and correcting hazardous, unsafe working conditions.

**Physical Demands:**

* Prolonged standing and walking, including interior and exterior security patrols
* Walking throughout buildings, parking areas and exterior grounds
* Lifting and carrying more than 20 lbs
* Wearing a tactical/security uniform )and protective vest (20lbs weight )during the shift
* Working indoors and outdoors in varying environmental conditions, including heat and cold
* Sustained attention, concentration and situational awareness
* Monitoring buildings, security systems and surrounding areas
* Responding to emergencies and other high-pressure situations
* Responding appropriately to unauthorized or suspicious individuals
* Conflict resolution and interaction with potentially non-compliant individuals
* Parking enforcement, traffic control and vehicle screening where applicable
* Escorting and continuously monitoring contractors within secured areas
* Where lawful, authorized and required, participating in or conducting an arrest in accordance with section 494 of the Criminal Code, which may involve physical exertion, close physical interaction, resistance, conflict and other high-pressure circumstances
* Regular keyboarding and record keeping in written logs required.

Pay: $31.00-$35.00 per hour

Expected hours: 40.0 per week

Benefits:

* On-site parking

Work Location: In person
